# Build context excludes. Both images build with `context: ..` (the repo root,
# docker-compose.yml), and neither COPYs the source tree: `src/` is bind-mounted
# at run time. What is actually COPYed is only
#   docker/prebuilt/*.deb, docker/entrypoint.sh, docker/scripts/, docker/cyclonedds.xml,
#   src/wuji-retargeting, src/wujihandros2/external/wuji-description/.../urdf,
#   src/unitree_sdk2_python (the g1_world_output image),
#   src/output_devices/g1_world_output/docker/entrypoint.sh
# so everything below is context the daemon would tar up and then never read.
# Without this file the context is ~2.9 GB, which is both slow and a real problem
# on a full disk; with it, well under 300 MB.

# Reference data and run artifacts (all gitignored, none of it COPYed).
RobotSTAR_demos/
wuji_runs/
wuji_clips/
clips/
sanitized_clips/

# History.
.git/
.gitattributes

# Docs and notes.
docs/
*.md
LICENSE

# Build and install trees, if a host-side colcon ever wrote them here.
build/
install/
log/

# Python and editor droppings.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.venv/
**/venv/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Vendored source that no COPY reads. The two paths that ARE read are
# re-included below, and order matters: the negations must follow the excludes.
src/
!src/wuji-retargeting/
!src/wujihandros2/external/wuji-description/hand/body/urdf/
!src/unitree_sdk2_python/
!src/output_devices/g1_world_output/docker/

# ...but not those trees' own history or caches.
src/wuji-retargeting/.git
src/wujihandros2/.git
src/unitree_sdk2_python/.git
**/wuji-retargeting/**/__pycache__/
